        what: "render/swiftShaderPass.js's bcs_hash (24 call sites) and render/voxelrenderer.js's cs_hash are the classic fract(sin(dot(p, C)) * K) shader hash. tools/ship/swiftShaders-selfcheck.mjs's OWN v4196 header already measured the cost: 'The sin-hash diverges by up to 0.68 on a 0..1 value between float64 and float32 -- not a rounding difference, a different random number,' and names it as the reason five of the fourteen ported shaders 'CANNOT agree with their CPU reference, ever.' That is a standing, accepted limitation in a gate whose whole convention is grading a GPU pass against a JS model to 0 or 1 of 255.",
        how: "skeeto/hash-prospector (Unlicense/public domain, github.com/skeeto/hash-prospector) exhaustively measures integer hash bias rather than eyeballing it, and publishes triple32 (3-round xorshift-multiply, exact bias 0.0209, near the theoretical limit) and the cheaper lowbias32 (2-round, bias 0.174) -- both 4-6 lines, pure u32 XOR/shift/multiply, no transcendental, so bit-exact across f32/f64 and across devices BY CONSTRUCTION the same way this arc's Philox work is. Not a dependency to add: the construction is small enough to hand-transcribe into bcs_hash's GLSL and its CPU mirror in render/swiftShaderModel.mjs, the same twin-implementation convention every other shader here already follows.",
        why: "This is not a stylistic nitpick -- it is the exact gap swiftShaders-selfcheck.mjs's own boundary names as permanent under the current hash, on code this arc did not touch (krispuckett/SwiftUIShaders ports). Replacing the hash would very likely: (1) turn 'cannot ever agree with CPU reference' into fixable for those five (and however many of the 24 call sites hit the same wall), (2) remove a real cross-device consistency risk this tree cares about everywhere else (SwiftShader vs real hardware, WebGPU vs WebGL2), since sin() at a deliberately large scaled argument is precision-sensitive by the nature of range reduction, and (3) likely read better -- the sin/fract hash's banding is a well-documented artifact, not a matter of taste. NOT the same move as render/worleyWgsl.mjs's hashU, which is deliberately bit-pinned to world/worleyBiomes.js's existing _hash for baked/seeded biome reproducibility -- changing THAT hash's arithmetic would reshuffle every already-seeded world's climate map, a correctness break rather than a quality gain, so it is explicitly NOT part of this item.",
        upstream: "no gate is currently red over this -- the divergence is accepted and bounded, not failing -- so nothing forces the round. Scope before starting: bcs_hash's ~24 call sites in render/swiftShaderPass.js, its CPU mirror in render/swiftShaderModel.mjs, and re-verification against tools/ship/swiftShaders-selfcheck.mjs plus whatever of postChain-selfcheck.mjs, solidTexture-selfcheck.mjs, voxelParallax-selfcheck.mjs and commentFalsePass-selfcheck.mjs pin its pixel output.",
