        blocker: "OPEN",
        what: "donmccurdy/mikktspace-wasm (MIT) is a WASM compile of MikkTSpace, the vertex tangent-space generation algorithm the glTF 2.0 spec itself recommends for normal-mapping correctness across engines/tools -- it is the de facto standard specifically because ad hoc per-engine tangent generation produces visibly different normal-map results on the same asset in different viewers. Checked against this tree's own code FIRST: a tree-wide grep for `mikktspace`, `MikkTSpace`, and `computeTangent` across every .js/.mjs file (excluding vendor/node_modules) returned zero hits -- there is no tangent-generation code anywhere in this tree. Not proven to cause a visible defect: three.js's built-in derivative-based fallback (computeVertexNormals-adjacent, no tangent attribute needed) 'works well for most assets' per MikkTSpace's own README, and no normal-mapping artifact has actually been observed or measured here.",
        how: "Requires unindexed/unwelded triangle input (one unique vertex per triangle corner, matching how MikkTSpace's reference C implementation walks the mesh) -- would need BufferGeometryUtils-style de-indexing before calling it and re-indexing after, the same shape of pre/post-processing xatlas-curved-uv-unwrap already needs for its own WASM call.",
        why: "A genuine, verified absence (zero hits, not an assumption) but a speculative fix -- logged because it is the spec-recommended standard and the gap is real, not because any asset in this tree has shown a wrong or seam-mismatched normal-map result under the current derivative-based fallback.",
        upstream: "no established want yet -- no gate or visual comparison has flagged a normal-mapping discrepancy attributable to tangent generation. Logged so the standard technique and its exact WASM binding are on file if such an artifact is ever found on an imported asset with authored normal maps.",
